# Document reconciliation

- Reconciliation is a versioned business workflow, not an unconstrained chat prompt.
- Pipeline: select source sets → parse/OCR → normalize → candidate match → deterministic checks → LLM-assisted classification/explanation → human review → export.
- Code performs arithmetic, totals, tolerances, dates, currency normalization, duplicate detection, and policy rules.
- LLM may suggest mappings or explanations but never becomes the sole authority for financial correctness.
- Preserve each normalized field’s source document, page/sheet/cell/range, raw value, normalized value, parser confidence, and transformation version.
- Matching rules are explicit, versioned, testable, workspace-scoped, and configurable only through authorized admin workflows.
- Every discrepancy has type, severity, deterministic evidence, suggested explanation, confidence, reviewer state, and citations.
- Low OCR confidence, ambiguous counterparties, conflicting currencies, missing pages, and formula errors must surface as review blockers.
- A reviewer sees side-by-side source evidence and exact normalized values before accepting a result.
- Approval binds the selected document versions and reconciliation rules hash; source changes invalidate pending approval.
- Export includes run ID, inputs, rule/model/parser versions, reviewer, timestamps, accepted/rejected differences, and checksums.
- Never write to 1C/ERP/DMS from reconciliation without a separate approved action proposal.
- Make runs idempotent and resumable. A retry must not duplicate adjustments, exports, or integration writes.
- Create golden fixtures for invoices, acts, statements, contracts, spreadsheets, scans, rounding, VAT, duplicates, and adversarial text.
- Measure field extraction accuracy, match precision/recall, false acceptance, review time, and unresolved rate.
